0.athena.sase-aq.1","local_name":"sase-aq.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-aq","agent_clan_generation":"20260729090844","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-aq.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-aq[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Keyed `{@<id>}` agent-name markers for xprompt swarms[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every `@` reference inside one xprompt swarm launch resolves to the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]same concrete agent-name token, chosen once per launch and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]substituted into the prompt text before any agent spawns, so a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]later swarm launch can never steal an earlier swarm's hood.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agent_name_key_markers.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-aq[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-aq/[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #87AFFF][/dim]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keyed marker grammar in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]grammar: teach `sase_core::agent_name_template` the `{@<id>}` / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`{@<id>!}` marker, add a lexical marker scanner and key accessor, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expose both through the `sase_core_py` bindings.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python facade and prompt-grammar plumbing[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]facade[dim] · [dim][/dim]after grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]facade: wrap the new Rust entry points in `sase.agent.names`, widen the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]directive and xprompt argument character classes so braced markers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]survive parsing, and bump the `sase-core-rs` requirement window.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Launch-time key resolution and text substitution[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]resolve[dim] · [dim][/dim]after facade[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve: add a keyed marker resolver that allocates one token per key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under the agent-name lock and rewrites every occurrence in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch's segment text, wire it into the launch funnel, and reject [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]markers that reach a runner.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Per-invocation key qualification at swarm expansion[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]qualify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after resolve[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]qualify: rewrite unqualified `{@<id>}` markers to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`{@<xprompt>.<stamp>.<id>!}` while expanding an xprompt swarm so each [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invocation gets its own key space, leaving `!` markers untouched.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate existing xprompt swarms[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after qualify[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: convert the bare `@` markers in this repo's `reads` swarm and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the chezmoi `research_swarm` swarm to the keyed syntax, including the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose references.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document the keyed marker syntax[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after qualify[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: describe the keyed marker, its qualification rule, and the `!` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]override in the xprompt documentation and the xprompt catalog help [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-aq","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-aq.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-9e56bcb0fc68a22f24b5987be786772b","started_at":"2026-07-29T13:09:00.210436+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785332756,"sha":"79be1d53a316d326790a9421435edf2942481fd9","subject":"feat(agent): expose keyed agent-name markers in Python"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"e4d9fa269af4905dceceacad07596152450b15e631fbab55afd59a067427ada4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/chat.md","size_bytes":6188},"commits":{"digest":"cc4d13531efe8974708304af5f763b16505e5c87c557a1d8a901e48b99397e20","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/commits.json","size_bytes":232},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"ba88a2fe51877d2d27177500796554292222509e33df4fb82d2e08825aaf6732","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/meta.json","size_bytes":600},"prompt":{"digest":"318d7f29e4f3e8b8c200ef28131e1342a488f244cf257a54862dd94210064433","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/prompt.md","size_bytes":153},"state":{"digest":"9ea2f49d40e4cfdf2c0e5161372b7290e4be83c9760267b8e921879b0b3e7818","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-aq.2","local_name":"sase-aq.2","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-aq","ag